1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
Subs by Mkrm

2
00:01:32,680 --> 00:01:35,100
Jianghai successfully defends the hill once again!

3
00:01:35,560 --> 00:01:36,540
Monica, that was incredible!

4
00:01:43,720 --> 00:01:46,140
Chengnan holds the hill!

5
00:01:47,840 --> 00:01:49,020
I completely misjudged him.

6
00:01:49,560 --> 00:01:50,460
Even the Captain lost.

7
00:01:50,920 --> 00:01:51,620
How are we supposed to Compete?

8
00:01:51,880 --> 00:01:53,820
Coach, we're gonna lose this one for sure.

9
00:01:57,000 --> 00:02:00,000
Episode 21

10
00:02:30,760 --> 00:02:32,220
Phantom Light Wheel!

11
00:02:50,440 --> 00:02:52,380
Jianghai takes the Hill!

12
00:03:17,120 --> 00:03:19,260
Mini... that's my Mini!

13
00:03:32,200 --> 00:03:34,580
Let's Go!

14
00:04:15,580 --> 00:04:17,820
Jianghai holds the Hill!

15
00:04:40,640 --> 00:04:45,660
Go, Jacky!

16
00:05:05,320 --> 00:05:07,740
Go, Captain!

17
00:05:59,080 --> 00:06:00,540
It's over. We're done for.

18
00:06:01,960 --> 00:06:02,940
Ugh.

19
00:06:15,100 --> 00:06:18,300
I'll now announce the Match Results!

20
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:20,120
Wait a moment!

21
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:25,000
That's Leo!

22
00:06:35,080 --> 00:06:38,470
Referee, wait! We still have one more Player!

23
00:06:38,920 --> 00:06:40,440
Jianghai still has one more Player to Compete.

24
00:06:41,500 --> 00:06:42,580
The Match continues!

25
00:06:44,200 --> 00:06:45,180
Go!

26
00:06:47,840 --> 00:06:49,980
Go, Leo!

27
00:08:09,720 --> 00:08:13,020
Go, Chengnan!

28
00:08:47,080 --> 00:08:48,540
Phoenix Soars the Nine Heavens!

29
00:08:48,600 --> 00:08:49,800
Sky-Piercing Fire

30
00:09:06,280 --> 00:09:11,520
I declare the winner of this Match to be...

31
00:09:11,700 --> 00:09:13,200
The Jianghai Team!

32
00:09:16,360 --> 00:09:17,820
We Won!!!

33
00:09:21,160 --> 00:09:22,620
That's amazing!

34
00:09:25,960 --> 00:09:27,900
Yeah! We won!

35
00:09:34,120 --> 00:09:35,580
Quiet! Quiet! Settle down!

36
00:09:36,040 --> 00:09:37,980
Me? I saw this coming all along.

37
00:09:38,240 --> 00:09:39,900
Coach Tony's got real talent.

38
00:09:40,360 --> 00:09:43,260
That's why I asked him to step up and be your Coach.

39
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:45,660
My judgment's still pretty sharp, isn't it?

40
00:09:47,260 --> 00:09:50,460
Coach Tony, you did great. Absolutely fantastic.

41
00:09:50,620 --> 00:09:52,380
With you leading our Jianghai Team,

42
00:09:52,820 --> 00:09:56,700
I, as the Principal, couldn't be more at ease.
A 1000% at ease.

43
00:10:04,840 --> 00:10:05,790
You've all been working so hard lately.

44
00:10:05,800 --> 00:10:06,780
Yeah, It's not bad at all.

45
00:10:07,240 --> 00:10:08,670
The Kids have been Training really well.

46
00:10:08,680 --> 00:10:09,960
And they're being safe about it, too.

47
00:10:11,080 --> 00:10:13,020
You can put your minds at ease, Principal and parents.

48
00:10:13,180 --> 00:10:15,540
We'll be wrapping up our Training here
soon and heading back to the City.

49
00:10:17,800 --> 00:10:19,740
Coach Tony, once you return to the City,

50
00:10:20,200 --> 00:10:23,100
I believe the School's renovation work is almost finished.

51
00:10:23,560 --> 00:10:25,990
When it is, I'll make sure to arrange
a top-notch Training space for you.

52
00:10:26,440 --> 00:10:28,380
We're fully committed to improving
the kids' Training conditions.

53
00:10:29,320 --> 00:10:30,780
That's wonderful! Thank you so much!

54
00:10:31,240 --> 00:10:33,180
That's wonderful! As a parent,

55
00:10:34,120 --> 00:10:36,060
I'd like to pitch in however I can.

56
00:10:36,520 --> 00:10:38,460
From now on, all of Jianghai's Competition Uniforms

57
00:10:38,920 --> 00:10:39,900
will be provided by my Company.

58
00:10:40,940 --> 00:10:43,740
Thank you! Thank you so much!

59
00:10:44,680 --> 00:10:45,630
It's the least we can do.

60
00:10:45,640 --> 00:10:47,100
And me too!

61
00:10:47,260 --> 00:10:49,470
This time, I'm planning to make those drinks I gave you

62
00:10:49,480 --> 00:10:51,420
the Official Beverage for the Jianghai Team from now on.

63
00:10:51,880 --> 00:10:52,860
I'll provide them for free.

64
00:10:53,600 --> 00:10:55,710
This drink is a secret recipe from our Song Family.

65
00:10:55,720 --> 00:10:57,180
It's a special cooling concoction.

66
00:10:57,640 --> 00:10:59,550
It's perfect for Training in this blistering heat.

67
00:10:59,560 --> 00:11:00,970
It cools you down, quenches thirst, and builds stamina.

68
00:11:01,960 --> 00:11:03,880
Thank you, thank you!

69
00:11:04,500 --> 00:11:05,000
Yes, Thank you.

70
00:11:05,800 --> 00:11:06,780
Thank you, Parents.

71
00:11:07,240 --> 00:11:09,400
for all your care and support of
our School's efforts. Thank you.

72
00:11:10,600 --> 00:11:12,990
And if the Jianghai Team ever needs

73
00:11:13,000 --> 00:11:14,500
professional Coaching on Image and Presentation,

74
00:11:14,920 --> 00:11:16,860
I'll spare no effort in lending a hand.

75
00:11:17,320 --> 00:11:18,780
Thank you! Thank you Miss!

76
00:11:21,160 --> 00:11:24,060
Thank you! Thank you!

77
00:11:26,920 --> 00:11:28,830
Goodbye, Principal! Goodbye Everyone!

78
00:11:28,840 --> 00:11:30,300
Goodbye!

79
00:11:38,440 --> 00:11:39,390
They're really gone.

80
00:11:39,400 --> 00:11:40,860
Let's go. Come on.

81
00:11:49,960 --> 00:11:50,940
What's up?

82
00:11:51,880 --> 00:11:53,820
Coach, why didn't my Grandpa come?

83
00:12:03,400 --> 00:12:05,340
Your Grandpa said he had to practice his Diabolo,

84
00:12:05,800 --> 00:12:07,260
so he couldn't find the time.

85
00:12:08,660 --> 00:12:10,140
He asked me to tell you

86
00:12:10,780 --> 00:12:12,540
that he believes you're all grown up now,

87
00:12:12,700 --> 00:12:14,940
and you can handle your own problems just fine.

88
00:12:17,320 --> 00:12:19,860
An old man as open-minded as he is...

89
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:21,700
you really don't meet someone like that every day.

90
00:12:22,120 --> 00:12:24,060
I know. Grandpa wants me to learn

91
00:12:24,220 --> 00:12:25,980
how to stand on my own two feet.

92
00:12:27,880 --> 00:12:29,340
And that's not even the half of it.

93
00:12:32,380 --> 00:12:34,140
He's aware of everything that goes on.

94
00:12:35,080 --> 00:12:36,540
He's a very perceptive man.

95
00:12:37,960 --> 00:12:38,940
You probably don't even know this,

96
00:12:39,480 --> 00:12:43,930
but back when I was stressing out
about our funding falling through,

97
00:12:44,680 --> 00:12:45,660
it was your Grandpa who gave me the idea.

98
00:12:46,120 --> 00:12:49,500
He told me to use tough Training
to temper the Team members. He said

99
00:12:49,960 --> 00:12:51,900
this way, they'd not only hone their skills,

100
00:12:52,360 --> 00:12:56,220
but it would build their character, too.
It was a real eye-opener.

101
00:12:56,680 --> 00:12:58,580
So you and my Grandpa talked about all this?

102
00:12:58,800 --> 00:12:59,800
Yeah.

103
00:13:00,520 --> 00:13:02,460
I also know that you came back to China

104
00:13:02,920 --> 00:13:04,830
so you could search within our traditional culture

105
00:13:04,840 --> 00:13:06,760
for the true Eastern Spirit of Yo-Yo.

106
00:13:07,500 --> 00:13:08,400
Which means

107
00:13:08,680 --> 00:13:12,060
you want to use mental focus and
feelings to conquer raw speed.

108
00:13:13,960 --> 00:13:17,340
But that's no easy task.

109
00:13:18,280 --> 00:13:20,700
Yeah, it's a problem that's been bugging me for a while.

110
00:13:22,600 --> 00:13:25,020
You could always ask your Grandpa for more advice.

111
00:13:25,480 --> 00:13:27,900
My Grandpa? He doesn't even know how to Yo-Yo.

112
00:13:29,320 --> 00:13:30,750
The cultural roots...

113
00:13:30,760 --> 00:13:33,180
although different, they share the common principles.

114
00:13:34,120 --> 00:13:36,060
You'll understand that one day.

115
00:13:52,360 --> 00:13:54,300
Leo, you're absolutely incredible!

116
00:13:55,240 --> 00:13:57,660
How did you manage to show up
right at the crucial moment?

117
00:13:58,600 --> 00:14:00,540
Leo, you came back just in time!

118
00:14:01,960 --> 00:14:03,870
You came back at the most critical moment.

119
00:14:03,880 --> 00:14:05,820
It's like you've got some kind of 6th sense.

120
00:14:07,240 --> 00:14:08,700
That was all the Coach's Master Plan.

121
00:14:09,160 --> 00:14:11,100
The Coach orchestrated everything.

122
00:14:12,600 --> 00:14:14,460
Coach, what's going on?

123
00:14:14,920 --> 00:14:16,860
Coach, come on, tell us!

124
00:14:19,240 --> 00:14:24,620
Actually, I knew that once the Chengnan Team
had scouted our Signature Moves,

125
00:14:25,180 --> 00:14:27,900
it would be too late to change
our techniques on the fly.

126
00:14:28,360 --> 00:14:30,300
But only Leo and Mini had
been practicing their new moves

127
00:14:30,760 --> 00:14:33,660
at night, so the Chengnan Team had no idea about them.

128
00:14:34,120 --> 00:14:37,500
So the Coach agreed with Leo's suggestion and
decided to turn their own trick against them.

129
00:14:37,660 --> 00:14:40,380
We faked kicking Leo off the Team,

130
00:14:40,840 --> 00:14:41,860
all so that at the very last moment of the Match,

131
00:14:42,000 --> 00:14:45,000
Leo could swoop in and catch them completely off guard.

132
00:14:46,300 --> 00:14:49,500
Whoa, you almost had us completely fooled!

133
00:14:50,440 --> 00:14:53,340
Leo, so you leaving was all just an act?

134
00:14:54,080 --> 00:14:56,220
We were so upset about it!

135
00:14:56,680 --> 00:14:58,140
But Coach,

136
00:14:58,600 --> 00:15:00,540
how could you just forgive Leo for messing up like that?

137
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:03,870
Yeah, he didn't even have to write a self-reflection!

138
00:15:03,880 --> 00:15:05,340
You can thank me for that one.

139
00:15:05,600 --> 00:15:07,260
What do you have to do with it?

140
00:15:07,720 --> 00:15:08,700
It's got everything to do with me!

141
00:15:10,300 --> 00:15:14,460
Right now, only the Coach and I know the real story.

142
00:15:32,280 --> 00:15:33,150
Chef Zhou!

143
00:15:33,160 --> 00:15:34,140
Hey, Coach Sarah!

144
00:15:35,080 --> 00:15:37,020
You did an amazing job as the Host last time!

145
00:15:37,280 --> 00:15:37,980
Oh, you're too kind.

146
00:15:38,040 --> 00:15:39,420
I just felt bad for your Team.

147
00:15:39,680 --> 00:15:40,860
You guys almost had it.

148
00:15:41,800 --> 00:15:43,710
Well, that's just how Matches go.
There's always a Winner and a Loser.

149
00:15:43,720 --> 00:15:44,700
True, true.

150
00:15:45,160 --> 00:15:47,580
It's a shame all those clever tricks
your Players cooked up went to waste.

151
00:15:48,040 --> 00:15:49,020
What clever tricks?

152
00:15:49,480 --> 00:15:50,430
You didn't know?

153
00:15:50,440 --> 00:15:53,820
Let me tell you, those Kids of yours are really sharp.

154
00:15:54,280 --> 00:15:56,700
They came and borrowed our Kitchen staff's Work Uniforms.

155
00:15:57,160 --> 00:15:58,590
They said they needed to wear them

156
00:15:58,600 --> 00:16:00,540
to go check out the Jianghai Team's Training.

157
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:04,380
They said, "Know yourself and know your enemy,
and you'll never be defeated."

158
00:16:04,840 --> 00:16:06,300
They've really got some education, those Kids.

159
00:16:06,460 --> 00:16:08,190
Chef! They need you to serve this food out, quick!

160
00:16:08,200 --> 00:16:09,180
Alright, alright!

161
00:16:09,240 --> 00:16:11,580
I've got to run. Goodbye, Coach Sarah!

162
00:16:19,040 --> 00:16:21,660
What you did has disappointed me deeply.

163
00:16:24,520 --> 00:16:25,980
I'm sorry, Coach.

164
00:16:27,200 --> 00:16:29,340
When Coach Tony's Team first made their accusations,

165
00:16:30,080 --> 00:16:32,000
I assumed they were just biased against us.

166
00:16:32,200 --> 00:16:33,200
I was so angry.

167
00:16:35,080 --> 00:16:37,980
But it turns out, you actually went and did it.

168
00:16:38,920 --> 00:16:40,380
It was completely underhanded and dishonourable.

169
00:16:40,640 --> 00:16:41,820
You made me lose face.

170
00:16:42,080 --> 00:16:46,140
I only did it to make sure the
Chengnan Team could take the title!

171
00:16:46,600 --> 00:16:47,580
You're so presumptuous.

172
00:16:52,360 --> 00:16:55,260
It's exactly that kind of sneaky, opportunistic mentality

173
00:16:56,000 --> 00:16:58,140
that cost us the Match.

174
00:17:00,520 --> 00:17:02,940
A real Competition is about true Skill.

175
00:17:03,400 --> 00:17:05,820
It relies on the solid,
consistent training we put in every day.

176
00:17:06,760 --> 00:17:07,740
Trying to pull a fast one...

177
00:17:08,200 --> 00:17:11,100
even if it gets you a win, it's just a fluke.

178
00:17:12,040 --> 00:17:13,020
Do you understand?

179
00:17:14,920 --> 00:17:16,380
I understand.

180
00:17:18,760 --> 00:17:19,740
You need to remember this.

181
00:17:20,960 --> 00:17:24,540
External factors are the least
reliable things in the World.

182
00:17:25,480 --> 00:17:28,860
Your own true strength is the
only thing you can always count on.

183
00:17:46,120 --> 00:17:48,050
Do you know why I asked to speak with you today?

184
00:17:49,960 --> 00:17:50,940
I know.

185
00:17:52,360 --> 00:17:55,710
I got careless and let my guard down.

186
00:17:55,720 --> 00:17:59,100
That's how all our Team's Signature Moves got leaked,

187
00:18:00,220 --> 00:18:01,980
and we almost lost the Match.

188
00:18:03,400 --> 00:18:04,380
What else?

189
00:18:05,680 --> 00:18:07,260
I was arrogant.

190
00:18:09,000 --> 00:18:11,100
I wouldn't listen to anyone else's opinions.

191
00:18:13,000 --> 00:18:14,460
I made all the decisions myself.

192
00:18:16,340 --> 00:18:17,820
And...

193
00:18:18,760 --> 00:18:19,740
And?

194
00:18:22,400 --> 00:18:25,980
And I didn't do a good job of keeping the Team united.

195
00:18:28,540 --> 00:18:29,820
What else?

196
00:18:42,460 --> 00:18:46,620
It's clear you still aren't ready to
sincerely own up to your mistakes.

197
00:18:49,960 --> 00:18:51,420
As a Captain,

198
00:18:51,880 --> 00:18:54,780
you're arrogant and think you're above everyone else.
You ignore other people's ideas.

199
00:18:55,040 --> 00:18:57,190
You don't care about Team unity and you form cliques.

200
00:18:59,260 --> 00:19:00,990
And even that's not the worst of it.

201
00:19:01,000 --> 00:19:02,460
What I absolutely cannot tolerate

202
00:19:03,200 --> 00:19:04,860
is that because someone else's Skills are better than yours,

203
00:19:05,120 --> 00:19:09,190
you try to push them out. You're jealous of them.

204
00:19:13,660 --> 00:19:15,420
Do you know what this means?

205
00:19:15,680 --> 00:19:17,790
A person like that isn't fit to be a Captain.

206
00:19:17,800 --> 00:19:20,220
They're not even fit to be a Member of the Jianghai Team!

207
00:19:20,280 --> 00:19:22,620
If it weren't for Shawn,

208
00:19:25,560 --> 00:19:28,380
I almost actually drove Leo away for good.

209
00:19:28,840 --> 00:19:31,260
Just think about it. If that had really happened,

210
00:19:31,720 --> 00:19:34,140
losing one Match wouldn't have been a big deal.
But losing a great Team Member?

211
00:19:35,560 --> 00:19:38,940
That would have been a real disaster.

212
00:19:40,160 --> 00:19:43,260
Thank goodness Leo was willing to endure
that humiliation without complaint.

213
00:19:45,160 --> 00:19:48,540
Coach... I'm sorry.

214
00:19:55,240 --> 00:19:57,880
What Teddy did was completely out of line.

215
00:19:59,260 --> 00:20:00,540
He deserves to be kicked off the Team.

216
00:20:01,960 --> 00:20:04,860
And as Captain, you did nothing to
correct him. You just let it slide.

217
00:20:07,240 --> 00:20:09,180
You should be prepared to face punishment as well.

218
00:20:10,120 --> 00:20:11,580
Coach!

219
00:20:11,840 --> 00:20:13,500
Please don't kick Teddy off the Team.

220
00:20:14,440 --> 00:20:16,860
I was the one who put him up to it.

221
00:20:17,800 --> 00:20:23,580
I'm... I'm willing to leave the Jianghai Team myself.

222
00:21:22,000 --> 00:21:23,580
Captain!

